WEBVTT

00:06.381 --> 00:08.425
[pensive violin music playing]

00:08.509 --> 00:13.514
[Sarah] 16 September,
in the year of our Lord 1702.

00:14.348 --> 00:16.892
The wind has favored us on my journey.

00:17.768 --> 00:20.771
The crew informs me
we are soon to make port.

00:21.855 --> 00:24.024
I hear he is a great man.

00:24.525 --> 00:28.070
Please, Lord,
let him be kind and handsome.

00:28.987 --> 00:31.156
And make room in my heart
for his children.

00:32.783 --> 00:35.994
I thought my time for marriage had passed,

00:36.870 --> 00:38.455
but you had other plans.

00:38.539 --> 00:40.874
- [wave crashes]
- [ship creaks]

00:43.502 --> 00:45.379
Today I begin a new life.

00:46.088 --> 00:48.257
I am to wed a leader,

00:48.882 --> 00:49.883
an explorer,

00:49.967 --> 00:52.511
the founder of this island hamlet.

00:53.637 --> 01:00.435
I, Sarah Westcott, shall this day become
Mrs. Richard Warren.

01:01.645 --> 01:03.647
[grunting] Just missed the fog.

01:04.272 --> 01:05.440
Stroke of luck, I suppose.

01:05.941 --> 01:08.151
No getting in or out once it arrives.

01:08.861 --> 01:09.945
Straight to the church then?

01:12.239 --> 01:13.532
[Sarah] What is he like?

01:13.615 --> 01:15.701
Well, he's the reason we're all here.

01:16.493 --> 01:18.579
Everyone on this island
owes a great debt to that man.

01:19.162 --> 01:22.374
Fore he arrived, it was a place
with nothing but barren dirt.

01:22.457 --> 01:27.045
But today, blossoms on the trees,
food for every hungry mouth, mild winters.

01:27.129 --> 01:29.798
[chuckles] He controls
the weather, does he?

01:30.507 --> 01:31.508
What's that?

01:32.259 --> 01:35.095
He controls the weather,
does he? [chuckles]

01:35.679 --> 01:36.763
No.

01:37.598 --> 01:40.851
But a cold breeze cuts
half as quick… [grunts]

01:40.934 --> 01:43.562
…when you've got
a warm home and a strong coat.

01:46.190 --> 01:47.191
Who said that?

01:47.941 --> 01:48.942
Richard Warren.

01:50.235 --> 01:53.238
[ominous music playing]

02:04.917 --> 02:07.085
[villager coughs, groans]

02:09.338 --> 02:11.215
[villager coughing]

02:17.262 --> 02:19.264
[townsperson]
Have you no kin come with you?

02:20.682 --> 02:21.683
No.

02:22.351 --> 02:24.686
I had resigned myself
to the lot of a spinster.

02:25.187 --> 02:29.608
Perhaps the greater celebration may be me
no longer a charge on my father's purse.

02:29.691 --> 02:33.362
It's a rare blessing
to marry at such an age.

02:34.238 --> 02:36.740
Lucky the island proved too small
to furnish him a wife.

02:36.823 --> 02:39.409
He had no choice
but to look to the mainland.

02:40.160 --> 02:43.997
A man of stature doth require
a goodly wife to order his household.

02:45.415 --> 02:47.626
Is he a man of-of good repute then?

02:49.253 --> 02:50.712
- [knocks on door]
- [door opens]

02:53.006 --> 02:54.800
Sarah, my child,

02:54.883 --> 02:59.012
I am Pastor Collins,
shepherd of the flock here on this island.

02:59.096 --> 03:01.640
- Pleased to meet you, Pastor.
- And I, you.

03:01.723 --> 03:02.891
How was your journey?

03:02.975 --> 03:06.228
[sighs] Well, I-I… I arrived
in good order, for which I give thanks.

03:06.311 --> 03:10.399
It must seem to you a strange land,
and you a stranger in it,

03:10.941 --> 03:12.818
but know that you have friends here

03:12.901 --> 03:16.905
and the light of God to lift you up
whenever you feel alone.

03:18.532 --> 03:19.783
Thank you, Pastor.

03:22.119 --> 03:27.291
If you are ever in need, do not
think twice to come to me at any hour.

03:27.374 --> 03:30.711
I will do what I can, by God's grace.

03:32.754 --> 03:34.006
I will, Pastor.

03:35.132 --> 03:36.133
Good.

03:39.011 --> 03:40.220
[Collins] Oh.

03:41.013 --> 03:44.391
Richard has requested
to be part of the wedding vows.

03:44.975 --> 03:47.144
Something he's written himself.

03:47.728 --> 03:49.021
[chuckles]

03:49.104 --> 03:51.523
They are unique.

03:53.609 --> 03:54.610
Unique?

03:56.195 --> 03:59.531
Love is as strong as death.

04:00.699 --> 04:05.913
Many waters cannot quench love,
neither can the floods drown it.

04:05.996 --> 04:09.750
Richard, do you take
this woman to be your lawful wife?

04:15.255 --> 04:16.380
I do.

04:16.464 --> 04:19.927
Sarah, do you take
this man as your lawful husband?

04:20.969 --> 04:23.263
- I do.
- [Collins] For you, as his helpmeet,

04:23.847 --> 04:25.891
will be bound to him.

04:25.974 --> 04:29.978
You will agree to serve him
as the Reeve Prime of the colony,

04:30.062 --> 04:33.398
the handmaiden
to the Lord Island Protector.

04:37.486 --> 04:38.820
I do. I do.

04:42.824 --> 04:44.117
[Richard] Thomas,

04:44.201 --> 04:45.369
John,

04:45.452 --> 04:46.453
Cromwell,

04:46.537 --> 04:47.538
Holyoke,

04:47.621 --> 04:48.622
Frances.

04:48.705 --> 04:50.457
Wagon wheel took her finger.

04:50.541 --> 04:52.876
Children, your new mother.

04:55.337 --> 04:58.340
[sighs] 'Tis a blessing to meet you all.

05:00.425 --> 05:01.760
[chuckles] Has she a name?

05:03.846 --> 05:04.888
[Frances] Mary.

05:06.682 --> 05:07.683
Good name.

05:09.309 --> 05:10.978
But I think she's missing something.

05:15.649 --> 05:18.193
This brooch came from my mother.

05:21.196 --> 05:22.990
[Holyoke] Is there one for each of us?

05:23.490 --> 05:25.742
[stammers, sighs]

05:27.202 --> 05:30.956
P-Perhaps the morrow shall yield, uh,
further tokens. [chuckles]

05:31.039 --> 05:32.875
[church bell tolling]

05:35.502 --> 05:36.753
At such an hour?

05:41.216 --> 05:42.217
[tolling stops]

05:42.301 --> 05:44.595
[unsettling music playing]

05:44.678 --> 05:46.555
[Richard] Ensure no harm comes to them.

05:48.807 --> 05:51.310
Have you an errand
that requires my company?

05:51.393 --> 05:53.395
No, I have work that needs doing.

05:55.731 --> 05:56.899
On our wedding night?

05:56.982 --> 05:59.943
The burdens of leadership
ride my shoulders by day and by dark.

06:00.027 --> 06:02.029
See them all laid down to their rest.

06:06.408 --> 06:10.245
[Sarah] I set down these lines
for the first time as a married woman,

06:10.787 --> 06:15.876
though I confess when my mother spoke
of what to expect on my wedding night,

06:15.959 --> 06:17.961
she missed the mark.

06:19.004 --> 06:21.423
First, there are five children here.

06:22.174 --> 06:26.261
Second, my husband departed suddenly
with neither a caress nor a kind word.

06:27.471 --> 06:30.891
But Christ asks us not to despair,

06:30.974 --> 06:34.394
and I look with hope
to grow into the duties of a wife.

06:34.478 --> 06:35.646
[thud]

06:35.729 --> 06:38.023
[footsteps approaching]

06:38.106 --> 06:40.108
[eerie, tense music playing]

07:01.463 --> 07:02.464
Richard?

07:10.389 --> 07:11.640
Richard, are you home?

07:15.102 --> 07:18.105
[ominous music plays]

07:18.188 --> 07:19.940
[breathing heavily]

07:20.023 --> 07:21.108
Richard?

07:34.371 --> 07:35.372
Richard?

07:48.302 --> 07:49.303
[gasps]

07:50.012 --> 07:51.096
Leave me be.

07:51.680 --> 07:53.765
[breathing heavily]

07:59.688 --> 08:01.690
[music fades, ends]

08:22.753 --> 08:24.171
[townsperson] You're a watcher.

08:28.967 --> 08:30.135
I'm sorry?

08:31.261 --> 08:33.263
You like to watch other people,

08:33.347 --> 08:35.349
see into their business.

08:36.850 --> 08:38.434
Forgive me, what befell them?

08:39.520 --> 08:41.145
[townsperson] There's a plague upon us.

08:41.647 --> 08:44.483
A violent madness comes over the infected.

08:45.067 --> 08:47.069
[inhales sharply] Can they not be healed?

08:47.569 --> 08:49.029
Well, that's my husband.

08:49.738 --> 08:50.739
Town physician.

08:50.822 --> 08:52.199
He does what he can for them,

08:52.783 --> 08:54.701
gives them something to calm their nerves,

08:54.785 --> 08:56.870
but heal them? No.

08:57.704 --> 08:58.705
But don't worry.

08:59.456 --> 09:03.460
Richard Warren always says
the bad times will end.

09:05.212 --> 09:06.839
God be with you.

09:06.922 --> 09:08.841
[unsettling music playing]

09:08.924 --> 09:09.925
And with you.

09:17.099 --> 09:20.060
[houseguest] There's three more infected
this week since the fog.

09:20.143 --> 09:21.687
That makes 20 now in total.

09:22.479 --> 09:25.732
[Richard groans] I have warned them
to stay out of the foul air.

09:26.233 --> 09:28.443
[houseguest] Otis Stevens
tends to the sick every day.

09:29.778 --> 09:31.029
But he's not infected.

09:31.113 --> 09:32.614
[Richard] Well, not yet.

09:33.532 --> 09:36.577
They say they suffer
from some kind of mania.

09:37.369 --> 09:38.662
Should we be worried?

09:40.455 --> 09:41.456
No.

09:44.710 --> 09:47.754
[houseguest] Cornelius Evans was, uh,
the first to fall ill.

09:48.297 --> 09:50.132
At first, had no symptoms
beyond a headache.

09:50.841 --> 09:53.135
His wife gave him brandy.
He slept soundly, but…

09:53.635 --> 09:57.514
he woke always with
the same headache. Here. Hmm.

09:57.598 --> 09:59.057
[unsettling violin music playing]

09:59.141 --> 10:00.684
Five days like this.

10:01.476 --> 10:03.312
And his eyes
were yellow with spoiled moons.

10:03.395 --> 10:04.396
He changed.

10:04.479 --> 10:05.981
He was angry, confused.

10:06.064 --> 10:07.232
Otis saw him that very night.

10:07.316 --> 10:08.650
He told him to take a warm bath,

10:08.734 --> 10:10.819
and he thought to come back
with a draught in the morning.

10:11.486 --> 10:13.906
But by dawn, when Otis came back,

10:14.823 --> 10:17.159
he saw a knot of hair in the doorway.

10:18.202 --> 10:22.206
Went inside
and he found Cornelius on the ground.

10:24.041 --> 10:26.752
With his fingers inside his wife's skull.

10:27.336 --> 10:30.255
[screaming]

10:33.091 --> 10:35.093
[houseguest] The infections
are growing faster.

10:35.677 --> 10:37.679
It will soon overwhelm us.

10:37.763 --> 10:39.097
We must do something.

10:39.181 --> 10:41.475
- You must do something.
- [Richard] Sarah, um,

10:41.558 --> 10:43.894
would you take yourself to bed?

10:43.977 --> 10:45.604
[inhales sharply]

10:45.687 --> 10:47.189
But I haven't finished cleaning.

11:00.994 --> 11:03.497
[houseguest] They say that
you're in communion with this island,

11:03.580 --> 11:05.624
that-that you whisper to it. [stammers]

11:05.707 --> 11:07.835
You tame it. You turn it to your will.

11:07.918 --> 11:10.379
That you are the only reason we survived

11:10.462 --> 11:12.756
- the first years.
- [Richard] Hold your tongue.

11:12.840 --> 11:16.635
[houseguest] They say that you kiss
that necklace like it was a cross,

11:16.718 --> 11:18.136
but it's no cross, sir.

11:18.637 --> 11:20.264
What is it you hide in there?

11:20.347 --> 11:21.682
They say it is a covenant!

11:21.765 --> 11:23.684
- [grunts, yells]
- [clattering]

11:24.226 --> 11:26.186
- [blow lands]
- [groaning]

11:26.270 --> 11:28.272
[sinister, tense music playing]

11:29.940 --> 11:31.942
[groaning continues]

11:44.121 --> 11:45.414
[Richard inhales deeply]

11:45.497 --> 11:47.499
- [grunting]
- [groaning]

11:48.750 --> 11:51.587
[panting]

11:54.339 --> 11:58.385
[whimpering, sobbing]

12:00.345 --> 12:02.347
[footsteps approaching]

12:02.431 --> 12:03.432
[whimpers]

12:09.229 --> 12:11.356
[door creaks]

12:22.451 --> 12:23.535
[Sarah inhales sharply]

12:24.870 --> 12:27.623
- [breathes shakily]
- [rooster crows]

12:28.665 --> 12:29.875
[inhales sharply]

12:34.129 --> 12:36.131
[mysterious music playing]

12:38.258 --> 12:41.261
[breathing shakily]

12:45.974 --> 12:47.226
[gasps]

12:50.354 --> 12:51.438
[sighs]

12:54.775 --> 12:56.693
[breathing shakily]

13:34.523 --> 13:37.526
[breathes shakily]

13:40.320 --> 13:42.155
[breathes heavily]

13:43.574 --> 13:45.409
[ominous sting plays]

13:47.494 --> 13:48.495
[gasps]

13:50.664 --> 13:51.874
[whimpering, panting]

13:51.957 --> 13:53.458
[banging on door]

13:54.418 --> 13:56.170
[panting]

13:56.837 --> 13:58.630
Child, what ails thee?

13:58.714 --> 14:01.008
[breathes shakily, whimpers]

14:06.722 --> 14:10.976
I feel I have greatly mistaken
my course in coming here.

14:11.059 --> 14:12.769
[breathing shakily, whimpering]

14:13.812 --> 14:17.733
Though my days before were sorrowful…
[stammers] …I fared well enough.

14:17.816 --> 14:20.777
[sniffles] Perhaps the life of a…
of a childless woman without a husband,

14:20.861 --> 14:23.155
it is… it is… It is one I could…
I could come to bear…

14:23.238 --> 14:25.908
- Enj… Enjoy! Enjoy the role--
- Good woman, you are not making sense.

14:25.991 --> 14:28.952
Well, I-I am filled with terror,
Pastor! [whimpers]

14:29.036 --> 14:30.287
I saw him.

14:30.370 --> 14:33.040
I saw him murder Ezra Lowery.

14:34.625 --> 14:35.626
Is there a body?

14:35.709 --> 14:36.960
No… [sniffles]

14:37.044 --> 14:39.505
…but there's a… [stammers]
…hidden chamber beneath our home

14:39.588 --> 14:42.591
and-and Ezra's bloody cane therein. [sobs]

14:44.218 --> 14:45.969
You must be told the truth.

14:46.053 --> 14:47.471
[Sarah breathes shakily]

14:47.554 --> 14:50.057
Evil stalks this land.

14:50.140 --> 14:53.018
- There is a wrongness about.
- [inhales sharply, sniffles]

14:53.769 --> 14:56.939
I fear that the devil himself
has chosen your husband.

14:57.523 --> 14:59.399
For what cause, I cannot tell.

15:00.317 --> 15:01.902
Others share my belief.

15:03.028 --> 15:04.780
We fear Warren consorts with him.

15:04.863 --> 15:06.448
[sobs, sniffles]

15:06.532 --> 15:08.700
Villagers go missing
and they're never seen again,

15:09.284 --> 15:10.661
including his last wife.

15:10.744 --> 15:12.871
Oh, God. [breathes heavily]

15:12.955 --> 15:16.708
I cannot stay here a moment longer.
I want off this dreadful island.

15:16.792 --> 15:20.128
I am but four and ten years almost.
Allow me to wither in my father's attic…

15:20.212 --> 15:22.047
- Sarah. Sarah.
- …as my womanly destiny.

15:22.130 --> 15:25.050
- Sarah.
- [sobs]

15:25.133 --> 15:28.887
Know that God has chosen you
for a special purpose.

15:28.971 --> 15:30.013
[breathing shakily]

15:30.097 --> 15:33.725
You arrived on this island
not for the reason you thought,

15:33.809 --> 15:35.811
but for a greater one still.

15:36.395 --> 15:39.231
Thou art not alone.

15:40.190 --> 15:43.652
- [sighs, inhales shakily]
- When you retire to bed tonight,

15:45.070 --> 15:48.657
leave the front door unlatched
so that we may enter.

15:49.783 --> 15:50.784
[softly] To do what?

15:53.537 --> 15:55.372
What must be done.

15:57.791 --> 15:59.585
[banging on table]

15:59.668 --> 16:04.047
[Richard] No one understands
the burdens of leadership.

16:04.673 --> 16:07.384
They're conspiring against me,
and you know that.

16:07.467 --> 16:10.387
They are afraid.
The plague, the disappearances…

16:10.470 --> 16:11.763
Disappearances?

16:14.641 --> 16:15.893
What disappearances?

16:18.562 --> 16:20.022
Who have you been speaking with?

16:20.105 --> 16:21.315
I've spoken with no one.

16:21.398 --> 16:22.691
[stammers]

16:24.484 --> 16:26.236
[stammers] 'Tis nothing.

16:26.320 --> 16:27.779
I… [speaks indistinctly]

16:27.863 --> 16:30.824
[stammers] Forgive me,
I cannot make sense of my own…

16:30.908 --> 16:31.992
My own words.

16:34.953 --> 16:36.622
Take all the children upstairs.

16:37.539 --> 16:38.540
The…

16:39.166 --> 16:40.167
Children.

16:50.052 --> 16:52.054
[foreboding music playing]

16:53.722 --> 16:55.140
[Frances] Is something wrong?

16:58.852 --> 17:00.270
[whispering] All shall be well.

17:16.787 --> 17:19.790
[mysterious violin music playing]

17:32.970 --> 17:35.013
[door creaks]

17:36.139 --> 17:37.266
[door closes]

17:37.349 --> 17:40.435
- [breathing shakily]
- [footsteps]

17:44.565 --> 17:47.442
[footsteps approaching]

17:47.526 --> 17:48.527
[door creaking]

18:02.666 --> 18:05.294
[footsteps approaching]

18:31.111 --> 18:34.948
[panting]

18:40.412 --> 18:42.706
- [attacker grunting]
- [Richard groaning]

18:42.789 --> 18:44.166
[Sarah panting, whimpering]

18:44.249 --> 18:46.335
[tense, sinister music playing]

18:55.260 --> 18:56.261
[thuds]

19:06.146 --> 19:09.441
[footsteps]

19:13.695 --> 19:15.697
[panting]

19:25.749 --> 19:27.125
[gasps]

19:33.924 --> 19:36.927
[breathing heavily]

19:45.811 --> 19:47.813
[Richard] Did I not plainly forewarn you?

19:50.023 --> 19:52.526
For your own safety,
you must not leave this house again.

19:53.485 --> 19:55.904
Not to do the wash,
not to accompany the children.

19:55.988 --> 19:58.574
- [Sarah breathing shakily, whimpers]
- [shushes]

20:01.702 --> 20:05.038
Well, let no fear take hold.

20:06.707 --> 20:10.460
I will unearth the one
who bears this guilt.

20:10.544 --> 20:15.966
None may hide forever on an island
where there is no way out.

20:21.263 --> 20:22.431
I will protect us.

20:23.140 --> 20:25.726
[groaning]

20:28.645 --> 20:29.646
Go to our room.

20:30.480 --> 20:31.690
Pray.

20:33.192 --> 20:34.193
[sobs]

20:35.903 --> 20:37.321
[sobs, groans]

20:42.868 --> 20:46.330
Oh, please. Oh, please.
[sobs] Oh, Father, please.

20:46.413 --> 20:50.042
[sobs] Please. [sniffles]

20:50.125 --> 20:52.127
[panting]

20:58.509 --> 21:00.427
[screams]

21:00.511 --> 21:02.596
[ominous music plays]

21:43.720 --> 21:47.558
[breathing shakily]

22:06.410 --> 22:09.413
[pants, breathes heavily]

22:16.879 --> 22:18.881
[ominous music plays]

22:31.018 --> 22:33.020
[gasps, breathes shakily]

22:54.124 --> 22:56.376
[whimpers, breathes shakily]

23:03.425 --> 23:04.426
[grunts]

23:04.927 --> 23:07.095
[breathes shakily]

23:08.055 --> 23:09.598
[gasps]

23:10.140 --> 23:13.143
[breathing heavily]

23:22.194 --> 23:23.320
[whimpers]

23:46.593 --> 23:50.180
[gasps, panting]

23:50.264 --> 23:52.516
[ominous music intensifies]

23:52.599 --> 23:53.767
[whimpering, panting]

23:58.480 --> 23:59.648
[whimpers]

24:03.819 --> 24:05.237
[breathing heavily]

24:06.280 --> 24:07.531
[grunts]

24:07.614 --> 24:10.450
[straining]

24:15.080 --> 24:16.081
[yelps]

24:17.583 --> 24:18.792
[panting]

24:21.879 --> 24:22.880
[door unlocks, opens]

24:22.963 --> 24:25.257
Pastor Collins! [panting]

24:25.340 --> 24:27.968
Richard is alive!

24:30.846 --> 24:33.724
Yes, we noted that with some distress.

24:33.807 --> 24:35.350
[breathes shakily]

24:35.434 --> 24:37.769
Be not afraid.
This committee can be trusted.

24:37.853 --> 24:39.605
Oh, then you all must listen.

24:39.688 --> 24:41.523
He is not consorting with the devil.

24:41.607 --> 24:43.025
He is the devil.

24:43.108 --> 24:45.944
I saw him struck with a knife again
and again, but he died not.

24:46.028 --> 24:48.864
For the good of every man, woman,
and child, you must make haste

24:48.947 --> 24:50.490
and stop him immediately.

24:50.574 --> 24:51.575
[sighs]

24:52.701 --> 24:54.912
[clicks tongue] There's a secret tunnel
that leads to the house.

24:54.995 --> 24:58.248
There's a well at the far southeastern
edge that will grant to serve you passage.

24:58.332 --> 25:00.834
You must send ten good, strong men.

25:00.918 --> 25:02.336
[sniffles, pants]

25:05.672 --> 25:08.926
A merchant sailing vessel
is due to depart this evening

25:09.009 --> 25:10.886
with a berth for you on it…

25:10.969 --> 25:12.262
[sighs] God be thanked.

25:12.346 --> 25:15.265
…but we need your help.

25:19.061 --> 25:24.566
Pour this in his drink,
and he will be helpless as a babe.

25:24.650 --> 25:26.652
No, I cannot go back there.

25:26.735 --> 25:29.488
You must, or he shall know.

25:30.364 --> 25:35.202
You said he must be stopped.
Now you bear the burden as well.

25:35.285 --> 25:38.121
[townsperson] Consider the welfare
of your children.

25:38.789 --> 25:42.709
[clicks tongue] My children?
I have but just met them.

25:42.793 --> 25:44.795
Sarah, please.

25:45.337 --> 25:49.174
You are our only hope
against this darkness.

25:49.258 --> 25:51.009
[breathes shakily]

25:52.469 --> 25:54.471
[ominous music plays]

25:54.555 --> 25:57.808
[Sarah] I do not comprehend
the nature of the curse

25:57.891 --> 25:59.643
that has fallen on the island.

26:00.435 --> 26:06.608
I do know that its heart beats inside the
cylinder my husband wears around his neck.

26:07.359 --> 26:08.777
Who will crush my throat?

26:08.861 --> 26:11.905
His hands? This plague?

26:11.989 --> 26:15.993
Death comes for us each,
but I-I fear to me first.

26:16.785 --> 26:18.620
I know not how, but who.

26:21.290 --> 26:22.291
[sniffles]

26:28.505 --> 26:33.427
Of course, he's here with me,
so I say all this in jest.

26:34.011 --> 26:36.096
And with that, I retire.

26:46.481 --> 26:48.066
You're home. What a blessing.

26:49.735 --> 26:51.778
What do you write in that book?

26:53.071 --> 26:54.781
A woman's silly thoughts.

26:56.700 --> 26:57.951
I want to read it.

26:59.244 --> 27:00.829
[Sarah] I would feel too abashed.

27:28.315 --> 27:30.317
A swig of brandy to ease your mind.

27:32.194 --> 27:34.112
[Richard] No, I need to be clearheaded.

27:41.537 --> 27:42.913
Go to your beds now, children.

27:42.996 --> 27:46.083
Now. I need a quiet word with your father.

27:47.668 --> 27:48.669
Now.

28:00.472 --> 28:02.474
[sighs]

28:05.853 --> 28:11.775
If folk are truly set against you,
you need your wife at your side.

28:14.820 --> 28:15.821
[sighs]

28:15.904 --> 28:18.365
We are married all these days
and have not yet…

28:21.285 --> 28:22.452
known each other.

28:28.333 --> 28:32.796
Well, the burdens that have
been placed upon me--

28:32.880 --> 28:34.882
Let me help you bear them.

28:34.965 --> 28:36.383
[Richard groans]

28:38.051 --> 28:40.888
[moaning]

28:48.187 --> 28:50.856
[moaning]

29:08.040 --> 29:10.709
- What sin lies on your tongue?
- [clicks tongue] Uh…

29:11.835 --> 29:12.878
[groans]

29:12.961 --> 29:16.089
You're in league with them. Traitress.

29:16.173 --> 29:17.925
[groaning]

29:20.344 --> 29:21.595
[groaning]

29:24.097 --> 29:25.933
- [grunts]
- [gasping]

29:27.017 --> 29:29.019
[coughs, pants]

29:31.563 --> 29:32.731
He killed my mother.

29:35.025 --> 29:36.944
Gather your siblings. We're leaving.

29:37.027 --> 29:39.446
[intense music plays]

29:44.201 --> 29:45.452
[Frances] Who are they?

29:45.536 --> 29:46.703
Just keep moving.

30:02.845 --> 30:04.263
[Sarah, children panting]

30:09.434 --> 30:10.644
They left without us.

30:10.727 --> 30:11.770
[pants]

30:11.854 --> 30:14.273
Here, into this boat. We can catch them.

30:14.982 --> 30:15.983
Easy.

30:23.365 --> 30:24.908
[townsperson] Are you leaving?

30:24.992 --> 30:25.993
[gasps]

30:27.202 --> 30:28.412
Abigail, I…

30:29.454 --> 30:31.290
I reckon you are not well.

30:31.957 --> 30:33.584
Go to your husband, the physician.

30:34.585 --> 30:35.794
I did already.

30:39.464 --> 30:41.258
I will get on board with you.

30:41.341 --> 30:43.427
I'm sorry, there-there
is not enough space.

30:44.469 --> 30:46.680
- [pants]
- But I am not sick!

30:48.557 --> 30:50.142
Forgive me, there is no space.

30:50.684 --> 30:53.520
Then leave off these children.
They're not of thy blood.

30:56.064 --> 30:57.065
They're with me.

30:57.149 --> 30:58.400
[breathes heavily]

30:59.526 --> 31:01.069
And under my charge.

31:03.780 --> 31:07.451
Stand back! I will take no more orders!

31:07.534 --> 31:09.244
[pants]

31:11.747 --> 31:13.916
[screams]

31:17.252 --> 31:21.882
[gasping] Go. Go. The ropes. [pants]

31:25.636 --> 31:28.847
[groaning]

31:35.896 --> 31:37.022
Traitors.

31:40.234 --> 31:44.071
You've set yourself above
the law of God and man.

31:44.154 --> 31:48.158
You have murdered
those you swore to protect.

31:49.368 --> 31:50.369
No!

31:51.036 --> 31:53.163
It doesn't want you to open it.

31:53.247 --> 31:55.791
What does not want me to open it?

31:56.375 --> 31:58.126
That which has kept us alive.

31:59.127 --> 32:02.965
It is just as we feared.
You have made a deal with the devil.

32:03.048 --> 32:05.217
No, it's not the devil.

32:05.843 --> 32:07.427
It is our God.

32:07.511 --> 32:10.931
He's gone mad. Let us be rid of him.

32:11.014 --> 32:12.516
You cannot rid yourself of me.

32:13.517 --> 32:15.018
It won't allow it.

32:15.102 --> 32:17.521
This is my burden.

32:18.438 --> 32:23.402
Free me, you will all be forgiven,
and I will continue to carry it myself.

32:23.485 --> 32:29.199
Your fate will be decided by God,
the one true God.

32:29.283 --> 32:32.619
[chuckles]

32:32.703 --> 32:33.912
[groans]

32:37.040 --> 32:42.004
No. You cannot bury me!
You cannot bury me!

32:43.380 --> 32:45.883
You'll doom yourselves! The pact!

32:46.383 --> 32:48.218
The pact must be honored!

32:48.302 --> 32:51.847
The pact which spared us… [pants]
…in that first winter.

32:51.930 --> 32:55.017
[pants] It spoke to me
through the mushrooms!

32:56.101 --> 32:58.353
Please. Fulfill the pact.

32:58.437 --> 32:59.646
How?

32:59.730 --> 33:01.773
Sacrifice! A life…

33:01.857 --> 33:03.567
Life for life. [pants]

33:04.276 --> 33:09.448
Whatever I have undertaken,
it has been for the welfare of our people!

33:09.531 --> 33:14.953
[groans] Fulfill the pact
and the plague will stop!

33:15.913 --> 33:17.122
But if you don't…

33:17.706 --> 33:18.832
If you do not,

33:20.417 --> 33:22.544
the terrors will not cease!

33:22.628 --> 33:24.254
They will only deepen!

33:24.338 --> 33:28.383
Please do not make my children
suffer for your mistake.

33:29.051 --> 33:33.055
Your wife is taking your children
back to the mainland, far from you.

33:34.848 --> 33:37.226
No. No, no, no.

33:37.309 --> 33:39.645
The island won't…
The island won't let them leave.

33:40.562 --> 33:42.314
Oh, please! Oh, please!

33:42.397 --> 33:44.441
You'll kill them all!
You'll kill them all!

33:45.526 --> 33:48.320
[yells]

33:48.820 --> 33:51.615
You'll kill them all!

33:51.698 --> 33:56.203
You'll kill them all!
You'll kill them all!

33:56.286 --> 33:58.330
You'll kill them all!

33:58.997 --> 34:03.752
You'll kill them all!
You'll kill them all!

34:03.836 --> 34:07.005
You'll kill them all!

34:08.966 --> 34:13.804
[Richard breathing heavily]

34:20.143 --> 34:23.146
["Brandy (You're a Fine Girl)" playing]

34:28.443 --> 34:31.071
[music continues]

34:37.202 --> 34:40.205
[grunting, panting]

34:57.139 --> 34:59.558
[moaning]

35:00.517 --> 35:02.978
[groaning, panting]

35:18.202 --> 35:20.537
- [grunting]
- [thuds]

35:23.332 --> 35:26.752
I got it. [grunts]

35:26.835 --> 35:27.836
[music continues]

35:27.920 --> 35:29.505
- You got it?
- Come on.
